# Automatic layers: autolayer

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for
[`autolayer()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/autolayer.html) has no examples, so this
notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`autolayer()` makes a ggplot2 layer for an object of a particular class in a single call, the
class deciding which layer, to be added to a plot. ggplot2 defines it as an S3 generic, and other
packages write methods for their own classes, as ggplot2's `automatic_plotting` page describes.
Not in Giggly yet: `autolayer()`.
